      "html": "<section class=\"ch wrap\"><div class=\"g4\"><div><div class=\"num\">01</div><div class=\"lab\">Overview</div></div><div class=\"c3\"><h2 class=\"h2\">The project in six numbers, and the three findings behind them.</h2><div class=\"mod\"><div class=\"cards\"><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"k\">Public documents read</div><div class=\"n\">9</div><div class=\"t\">Swiggy's own policy pages, the starting point for every rule</div></div><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"k\">Insights kept</div><div class=\"n\">6</div><div class=\"t\">Each backed by at least three kinds of evidence</div></div><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"k\">Ideas tested</div><div class=\"n\">34</div><div class=\"t\">Every idea checked against six questions</div></div><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"k\">Playable tickets</div><div class=\"n\">5</div><div class=\"t\">A coded prototype, from hand-over to a closed ticket</div></div><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"k\">Findings</div><div class=\"n\">16</div><div class=\"t\">From a heuristic evaluation, none blocking a decision</div></div><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"k\">Tickets with no verdict</div><div class=\"n\">5 of 5</div><div class=\"t\">Nothing on screen recommended, scored or predicted</div></div></div><div class=\"rows n3\" style=\"margin-top:56px\"><div class=\"r\"><div class=\"i\">1</div><div>No platform publishes what a human reviewer's screen looks like, and Swiggy is no exception.</div></div><div class=\"r\"><div class=\"i\">2</div><div>Up to 25% of refunds in a Swiggy-group study went wrong, mostly because of weak photo evidence.</div></div><div class=\"r\"><div class=\"i\">3</div><div>Training cannot stop people over-trusting automated advice, so the screen shows facts and never a verdict.</div></div></div></div></div></div></section>"
