      "html": "<section class=\"ch wrap\"><div class=\"g4\"><div><div class=\"num\">04</div><div class=\"lab\">Research</div></div><div class=\"c3\"><h2 class=\"h2\">No one inside could be reached, so the rules were rebuilt from what is public.</h2><p class=\"lead\">No Swiggy agent, internal policy or real case data was available. Seven methods filled the gap, and every rule found was tagged by where it came from.</p><div class=\"mod\"><div class=\"bign\"><div><div class=\"n\">9</div><div class=\"t\">public Swiggy documents read</div></div><div><div class=\"n\">29</div><div class=\"t\">published rules found in them</div></div><div><div class=\"n\">7</div><div class=\"t\">notes on reading them safely</div></div><div><div class=\"n\">9</div><div class=\"t\">gaps no public source covers</div></div></div><div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"st\">Every rule carries its source</div><div class=\"legend\"><span><b><span class=\"pill \">Published</span></b>Swiggy's public documents</span><span><b><span class=\"pill \">Law</span></b>Indian law</span><span><b><span class=\"pill \">Adapted</span></b>another platform's published rule</span><span><b><span class=\"pill \">Owner</span></b>the project's own rule</span><span><b><span class=\"pill as\">Assumed</span></b>a placeholder, never Swiggy's policy</span></div><div class=\"tb \"><div class=\"r hd\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,110fr) minmax(0,620fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div>Code</div><div>Rule</div><div>Source</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,110fr) minmax(0,620fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>P4</b></div><div>On cash on delivery, the customer need not pay for a wrong or missing order reported before it is marked delivered</div><div><span class=\"pill \">Published</span></div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,110fr) minmax(0,620fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>P5</b></div><div>A photo-based complaint needs at least one customer photo the agent agrees with</div><div><span class=\"pill as\">Assumed</span></div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,110fr) minmax(0,620fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>P6</b></div><div>The restaurant's refund terms decide what it pays, and Swiggy pays anything above them</div><div><span class=\"pill \">Owner</span><span class=\"pill as\">Assumed</span></div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,110fr) minmax(0,620fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>T1</b></div><div>A refund above ₹500 is flagged for a second review</div><div><span class=\"pill \">Adapted</span><span class=\"pill as\">Assumed</span></div></div></div><div class=\"cap\">4 of the working set shown. The full set, with every source, is in the Agent Desk Handbook.</div></div><div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"st\">Seven methods, one real call</div><div class=\"tb \"><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,120fr) minmax(0,640fr)\"><div><b>Expert interview</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Primary</span></div><div>One 10-minute call with a customer-service expert at American Express. Expert opinion, not observed agent behaviour</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,120fr) minmax(0,640fr)\"><div><b>Simulated expert interview</b></div><div><span class=\"pill as\">Simulated</span></div><div>A composite expert answering only from public sources. 43 claims traced, none unsupported. Always labelled simulated</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,120fr) minmax(0,640fr)\"><div><b>Customer experience audit</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Primary</span></div><div>Complaints made on test orders, written up from two records of the test</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,120fr) minmax(0,640fr)\"><div><b>Secondary research</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Secondary</span></div><div>Swiggy's public documents, news, legal records and other platforms' rules</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,120fr) minmax(0,640fr)\"><div><b>Literature review</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Secondary</span></div><div>5 papers on automation bias, explanations and agent tools</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,120fr) minmax(0,640fr)\"><div><b>Artifact analysis</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Secondary</span></div><div>8 public artifacts, including Swiggy's engineering post and job listing</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,120fr) minmax(0,640fr)\"><div><b>Gap analysis</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Secondary</span></div><div>What no public source covers, sorted into types A to E</div></div></div></div><div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"st\">Expert view</div><div class=\"two\"><div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"q\">Everything on the agent's screen should help the agent reach a decision in less time.</div><div class=\"s\">Customer-service expert, American Express · paraphrased</div></div><div class=\"tb \"><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,150fr) minmax(0,335fr)\"><div><b>Policy</b></div><div>Insights shown to the agent are already based on policy</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,150fr) minmax(0,335fr)\"><div><b>Evidence</b></div><div>Evidence is shown in a way that is easy to take in. The format on this screen is our own reading</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,150fr) minmax(0,335fr)\"><div><b>Precedent</b></div><div>Show how a strong agent solved a similar problem. Moved to Ideation as reference cases</div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"st\">Customer experience audit</div><div class=\"tb \"><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,760fr)\"><div><b>Made-up claims</b></div><div>All refunded, in both records of the test, including one from a fresh account</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,760fr)\"><div><b>Genuine claims</b></div><div>Inconsistent. One record reports both refused, the other at least one refunded</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,760fr)\"><div><b>Not recorded</b></div><div>Exact dates, the refusal wording, whether the device changed, whether refunds were returned</div></div></div><div class=\"formal\" style=\"margin-top:36px\"><div class=\"k\">Statement</div>This audit was run to find the limits of Swiggy's existing customer support system. Some complaints were made up on purpose, and every made-up claim was refunded. It is reported as it happened, and no further made-up claims were made.</div></div><div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"st\">Precedents</div><div class=\"tb \"><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,560fr) minmax(0,200fr)\"><div><b>Uber Eats</b></div><div>Fault categories and review triggers</div><div><span class=\"pill \">Adapted</span></div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,560fr) minmax(0,200fr)\"><div><b>DoorDash</b></div><div>Refunds at the value of the affected item</div><div><span class=\"pill \">Adapted</span></div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,230fr) minmax(0,560fr) minmax(0,200fr)\"><div><b>Zomato</b></div><div>One opaque \"karma score\" for customers and riders</div><div><span class=\"pill g\">Avoided</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section>"
