      "id": "insights",
      "html": "<section class=\"ch wrap\"><div class=\"g4\"><div><div class=\"num\">05</div><div class=\"lab\">Insights</div></div><div class=\"c3\"><h2 class=\"h2\">Six insights, each kept only when three kinds of evidence agreed.</h2><p class=\"lead\">With no field data, agreement across different kinds of source was the test. An insight resting on inference alone was not kept.</p><div class=\"mod\"><div class=\"legend\"><span><b>O</b>Official</span><span><b>L</b>Law</span><span><b>R</b>Reported</span><span><b>A</b>Anecdotal</span><span><b>P</b>Primary</span><span><b>S</b>Simulated</span><span><b>Lit</b>Literature</span></div><div class=\"tb \"><div class=\"r hd\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,30fr) minmax(0,400fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr)\"><div></div><div>Insight</div><div>Evidence tiers</div><div>What it means for the screen</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,30fr) minmax(0,400fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr)\"><div><span class=\"i\">1</span></div><div><b>The policy lists the conditions but leaves the outcome to discretion</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Official</span><span class=\"pill \">Reported</span><span class=\"pill \">Primary</span><span class=\"pill \">Simulated</span></div><div>Each condition sits next to the fact it is checked against</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,30fr) minmax(0,400fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr)\"><div><span class=\"i\">2</span></div><div><b>Refund mistakes come mainly from weak evidence, not missing history</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Reported</span><span class=\"pill \">Primary</span><span class=\"pill \">Official</span><span class=\"pill \">Simulated</span></div><div>Evidence gets its own section, with origin and time</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,30fr) minmax(0,400fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr)\"><div><span class=\"i\">3</span></div><div><b>Wherever history is collected, it turns into one opaque score</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Reported</span><span class=\"pill \">Official</span><span class=\"pill \">Literature</span><span class=\"pill \">Simulated</span></div><div>History as dated counts per party, never a score</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,30fr) minmax(0,400fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr)\"><div><span class=\"i\">4</span></div><div><b>One decision shifts cost across three parties, yet the agent's view looks customer-only</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Official</span><span class=\"pill \">Reported</span><span class=\"pill \">Anecdotal</span></div><div>Who bears the cost, shown as a plain fact</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,30fr) minmax(0,400fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr)\"><div><span class=\"i\">5</span></div><div><b>Speed with no checks rewards the wrong cases</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Primary</span><span class=\"pill \">Anecdotal</span><span class=\"pill \">Reported</span><span class=\"pill \">Literature</span></div><div>Save time on looking up, never on checking</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,30fr) minmax(0,400fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr)\"><div><span class=\"i\">6</span></div><div><b>Rules and deadlines differ by source</b></div><div><span class=\"pill \">Official</span><span class=\"pill \">Reported</span><span class=\"pill \">Law</span><span class=\"pill \">Simulated</span></div><div>Every rule labelled with its source</div></div></div><div class=\"cap\">Dropped for fewer than three tiers. \"Agents can approve only up to a limit\" (inference only) and \"device signals feed refund decisions\" (one report).</div><div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"st\">Where thinking and policy pull apart</div><div class=\"strip\"><div class=\"\"><b>1</b>Reads the hand-over</div><div class=\"\"><b>2</b>Works out what went wrong</div><div class=\"\"><b>3</b>Checks when it happened</div><div class=\"\"><b>4</b>Looks for proof</div><div class=\"hot\"><b>5</b>Looks at past refunds</div><div class=\"\"><b>6</b>Decides who is at fault</div><div class=\"\"><b>7</b>Picks an amount</div><div class=\"hot\"><b>8</b>Assumes the restaurant agrees</div><div class=\"\"><b>9</b>Explains the outcome</div></div><div class=\"cap\">Inferred from research, no agent was observed. Steps 5 and 8 are the widest gaps. History weighs in but the policy never names it, and the restaurant's answer has no visible status.</div><div class=\"decin\"><div class=\"r\"><div class=\"k\">Decision</div><div>Show every party's history on screen as dated counts, labelled context and not a policy condition</div></div><div class=\"r\"><div class=\"k\">Reason</div><div>History already weighs in on the decision. Leaving it off the screen would hide that bias, not remove it</div></div><div class=\"hb\"><div>Agent Desk Handbook<span class=\"g\">H-10 · Party history</span></div><svg class=\"chev\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><path d=\"M4 2l4 4-4 4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg></div></div></div><div class=\"sec\"><div class=\"st\">Who carries the cost</div><div class=\"tb \"><div class=\"r hd\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,170fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div>Stakeholder</div><div>What a decision costs or gives</div><div>What they can see</div><div>Can they dispute it</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,170fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>Customer</b></div><div>Refund, coupon or denial</div><div>Chat and outcome, no reasons for a block</div><div>Outside Swiggy, helpline and consumer commissions</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,170fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>Escalation agent</b></div><div>Time, accuracy, accountability</div><div>Reported, customer profile and 3-month refunds</div><div>None</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,170fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>Restaurant</b></div><div>Deductions from payouts, liability for quality</div><div>Its own metrics, in a separate dashboard</div><div>Reportedly no route</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,170fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>Delivery partner</b></div><div>Fines, removal from the platform</div><div>Not documented</div><div>Not documented</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,170fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>Swiggy</b></div><div>Refund cost, fraud losses</div><div>Full data</div><div>Its decision is final</div></div><div class=\"r\" style=\"grid-template-columns:minmax(0,170fr) minmax(0,260fr) minmax(0,280fr) minmax(0,260fr)\"><div><b>Regulator</b></div><div>Enforces the law</div><div>Complaint volumes</div><div>Can override Swiggy</div></div></div><div class=\"cap\">The parties who carry the cost see the least and have the weakest way to dispute it.</div></div></div></div></div></section>"
